      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1373460489,
      "text": "Ficus petiolaris, commonly known as petiolate fig, rock fig, and amacóztic, is a fig that is endemic to Mexico from Baja California and Sonora south to Oaxaca. It grows best with moderate water and partial shade. A unique feature is white hairs on the vein axils. Other common names include the Baja California rock fig, Palmer wild fig, and Brandegee wild fig."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Ficus petiolaris",
